{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 1: LLM-Review +1 (PASS), Verified -1. Cause was NOT my change: the 'Git version floor gate' step failed with 'missing .github/git-version-floor.txt'. That file landed on main in 980d AFTER my branch base, and the Gerrit Verified lane takes the workflow DEFINITION from the target branch while checking out the CHANGE'S tree - the exact definition-vs-tree skew that _build-and-test.yml documents under ticket ee2a and guards against with an if-present check. The new floor gate did not copy that guard. Remedy: rebased onto current origin/main (now includes 980d and dce2); re-verified lock-check/install/lint/typecheck/metrics-degradation all green on the rebased tree; pushed patchset 2 keeping Change-Id Ifcbd4432."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785908801633869001,"uuid":"1da762fd-98cd-4b73-b702-13bbd4f01e48"}